From 39e6dca44f22405a9cc225ddb725492c15c2119e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:20:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: same definition of the behaviour class in host and
 device code

The parameters treated as static variables were declared as static
constexpr data members in host code and as constant data members in
device code: the class had different definitions in the host and device
compilations (CUDA, HIP), which breaks as soon as an object of the class
is built on the host and used on the device.

The requirement of a class usable in device code is now explicit:
- an interface states that it uses the behaviour class in device code
  (`requiresDeviceCompatibleBehaviourClass`, which replaces
  `areDynamicallyAllocatedVectorsAllowed`), the generic-parallel
  interface does;
- the behaviour description records the requirement
  (`requireDeviceCompatibleClass`): dynamically allocated vectors are
  not allowed and the parameters treated as static variables are
  declared as constant data members, in host and device code. Other
  behaviours are unchanged;
- behaviour variables inherit the requirement of the behaviour which
  uses them (new DSL option `device_compatible_class`).

A test behaviour with parameters treated as static variables, bound to
references, is added to all the configurations.
